---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const IMG = '/images/about';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="A bit about Ali Brown — inclusive product designer and researcher.">
	<article class="about">
		<section class="two-col">
			<div class="two-col-text">
				<h1>About me</h1>
				<blockquote class="pull-quote">I am an inclusive product designer and researcher.</blockquote>
				<p>
					People change, people have different needs, there is no one size fits all. This is one of the reasons I am
					drawn to design. I have a natural curiosity to understand people and their needs.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="two-col-image">
				<img src={`${IMG}/photo-1.png`} alt="Portrait of Ali" />
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="two-col">
			<div class="two-col-text">
				<h3>I believe that inclusive design is the key to good design.</h3>
				<p>
					When you design for the people in the margins, you create designs that benefit everyone. As a designer you
					need to challenge your own biases, this is something I do in both my professional and personal life.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="two-col-image">
				<img src={`${IMG}/photo-3.png`} alt="" />
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="two-col">
			<div class="two-col-text">
				<h3>Whatever work I do I always think about inclusivity, equity and accessibility.</h3>
				<p>
					I graduated from the Interaction Design program at Sheridan college in 2024, and for the last two years I have
					been working as a designer for <a
						href="https://makeitfable.com/"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">Fable Tech Labs<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a
					> where I was helping clients build accessible products with people with disabilities. My volunteer work has
					also helped me develop my skills in listening and learning from people. For two years, I volunteered at <a
						href="https://hollandbloorview.ca/"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">Holland Bloorview Kids Rehabilitation Hospital<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a
					> where I worked with teenagers with disabilities and, I&rsquo;m currently volunteering at <a
						href="https://www.varietyvillage.ca/"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">Variety Village<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a
					> where I&rsquo;m working with adults with developmental disabilities.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="two-col-image">
				<div class="crop-photo-4">
					<img src={`${IMG}/photo-4.png`} alt="" />
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="two-col two-col--last">
			<div class="two-col-text">
				<h3>Throughout my experiences I have found opportunities to listen, learn, unlearn and grow.</h3>
				<p>To me, this is essential to truly understanding people and good design.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="two-col-image">
				<img src={`${IMG}/photo-2.png`} alt="" />
			</div>
		</section>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about {
		background: var(--color-bg);
	}

	.two-col {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 3fr 2fr;
		align-items: center;
		gap: var(--space-5);
		padding: 0 var(--page-gutter);
		border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-light);
	}

	.two-col--last {
		border-bottom: none;
	}

	.two-col-text {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--space-4);
		color: var(--color-text-on-dark);
	}

	.two-col-text a {
		color: var(--color-light);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	.two-col-text a:focus-visible {
		outline: 2px dashed var(--color-light);
		outline-offset: 4px;
	}

	.pull-quote {
		margin: 0;
		padding: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
		border-left: 5px solid var(--color-accent-yellow);
		font-size: var(--text-h3-size);
		font-weight: var(--text-h3-weight-bold);
	}

	.two-col-image {
		aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 29.75rem;
		overflow: hidden;
		background: var(--color-light);
		justify-self: end;
	}

	.two-col-image img {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
	}

	/* Reproduces the specific off-center zoomed crop from Figma's "image 24"
	   layer, which doesn't fit the simple centered object-fit:cover treatment
	   used for the other photos on this page. */
	.crop-photo-4 {
		position: relative;
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
	}

	.crop-photo-4 img {
		position: absolute;
		width: 149.67%;
		height: 199.57%;
		left: -7.42%;
		top: -78.61%;
		max-width: none;
		object-fit: unset;
	}

	/* Sections are deliberately flush (no vertical padding) on desktop, but
	   that gets crowded once text and image are close together — and worse
	   once they stack. Add breathing room back for anything 900px and under. */
	@media (max-width: 900px) {
		.two-col {
			padding-top: var(--space-5);
			padding-bottom: var(--space-5);
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 800px) {
		.two-col {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
